WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.149
Maybe it's a mom putting her baby's life at
risk or a dad stopping his son from pursuing

00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:05.780
his dreams.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.940
Or maybe the parents are just straight-up
homicidal.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.850
Whether they're letting loose with emotional
abuse or trying to give their kids a permanent

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.120
timeout, these are the worst parents in movie
history.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.180
Marvel dads are the worst.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.620
They lie to their kids, disappoint them, and
in some instances, try to murder them.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.960
And they don't get any worse than Thanos,
the Mad Titan with terrible parenting skills.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.680
He's a purple warlord who wants to annihilate
half the universe, but he also fancies himself

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.660
a father figure.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.260
When he's not murdering entire planets full
of people, he's busy adopting kids to join

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.809
his little death cult.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:43.260
And by "adopting," we mean killing their parents
and kidnapping them.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:46.320
"Unh-uh.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.200
Concentrate."

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.160
Naturally, life with Thanos can be kind of
traumatizing, as he often forces his kids

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.380
to fight each other in bloody, brutal duels.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.980
He particularly enjoys torturing his daughter
Nebula, cutting off her body parts and replacing

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.200
them with hunks of metal.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.330
He may have fond feelings for Gamora but at
the end of the day, he throws her off a cliff

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.180
so he can get his hands on a shiny stone.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:12.300
When your rock collection is more important
than your own kids, it means you probably

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.220
weren't cut out for this whole adoption thing.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:20.600
Played to perfection by Allison Janney in
the biopic I, Tonya, LaVona Golden is a chain-smoking,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.150
hard-drinking, foul-mouthed devil woman.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.720
As the mother of ice skater Tonya Harding,
she does all sorts of horrible things to push

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.760
her little girl to glory.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.680
She nags her from the sidelines, violently
beats her, and forces her to skate so long

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.900
that she pees in the rink.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.320
Even when Tonya grows up, LaVona keeps going
with the put-downs.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.840
Every look she shoots her daughter is dripping
with anger and disdain.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.920
She won't even tell her daughter that she
loves her, probably because she doesn't love

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.300
anything except her cigarettes.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.500
Later on, she justifies her awful behavior
by saying:

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.300
"I made you a champion, knowing you'd hate
me for it.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.100
That's a sacrifice a mother makes."

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.700
But really, Golden just drives her daughter
towards a life of abuse and scandal.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.360
At first glance, Ego the Living Planet seems
like the perfect dad.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.240
He saves his long-lost son, Peter Quill, from
an army of bad guys.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.570
He invites him to live in a gorgeous paradise.

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.020
And he even looks like Kurt Russell.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.020
Sure, he hasn't been a part of Peter's life
for decades, but now they're reunited and

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.950
ready for an overdue game of catch.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:23.950
Alas, Ego is a godlike being who wants to
spread his seed across the universe, in more

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:24.660
ways than one.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:29.620
His plan involves planting extraterrestrial
flowers that will eventually transform entire

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.060
planets into extensions of his consciousness.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.520
"...until everything is me."

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:44.260
But he needs help carrying out his plan in
the form of another demigod with similar powers.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:48.940
So he goes around the universe, impregnating
basically every being he comes across.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.780
When his kids are all grown, he brings them
to his homeworld to see if they inherited

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.380
any of his Celestial abilities.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.560
If they haven't, he kills them and leaves
their remains in a cave full of bones.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.400
There are bad dads, and then there are straight-up
evil dads.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.760
Jack Torrance falls in the latter category.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.140
Played by Jack Nicholson in The Shining, Torrance
is a writer and a caretaker at the mountainside

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.120
Overlook Hotel.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.820
He starts off a little psycho and just gets
more unhinged as the film goes on.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:22.500
"Then I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow
your house in."

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.980
That psychosis isn't good for Jack's son Danny,
who possesses a psychic ability called "the

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.960
shining," that allows him to see all the evil
spirits lurking in the Overlook.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.660
But despite his powers, he can't stop his
dad from going completely insane, grabbing

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:42.180
an axe, and calling him over for some bloody
father-son bonding time.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.800
Jack chases little Danny all over the hotel
and out into the snowy hedge maze, where the

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:50.060
kid manages to outsmart and escape his dastardly
old dad.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.280
And in Jack's final moments, he learns that
trying to kill his kid does not make him a

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.000
cool parent.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.900
Well actually, it kind of does.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:03.760
Life can be hard when you're an introverted
teenager who's relentlessly bullied while

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.930
developing scary psychic powers.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.630
A girl like that really needs a mom to care
for her and guide her through those difficult

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.120
times.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.800
Unfortunately for Carrie White, her mother
is an absolute nut job who'd rather stab her

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:17.809
daughter with a butcher's knife than help
her figure out high school.

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:22.319
Played by Piper Laurie, Margaret White is
a psycho who wants to keep Carrie as isolated

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.500
from the world as possible.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.840
When Carrie has her first period, Margaret
locks her in a closet and forces her to pray

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.660
for forgiveness for her wicked ways.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.300
When she goes off to prom, Margaret does everything
she can to keep Carrie at home, telling her

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.340
all her classmates will just laugh at her.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.080
It all culminates in a candle-lit showdown
when Margaret looks a little too happy while

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.960
trying to stab her daughter to death.

